🌐 TCP Unit Conversion System

A lightweight multithreaded TCP client-server system built in Python that performs unit conversions over a custom text-based protocol.

🧠 Tech Stack
Language: Python 3.10+
Libraries: socket, threading (standard library only)
Architecture: TCP Client–Server (Multithreaded)
📁 Project Structure
Server.py   → TCP server (handles multiple clients via threads)
Client.py   → Interactive TCP client
Tests.py    → Automated test suite (21 test cases)
⚙️ How to Run
▶️ 1. Check Python Version
python3 --version
🖥️ 2. Run the Server
python3 Server.py

📍 Starts server on:

0.0.0.0:5000
Host & port can be changed via constants in Server.py
Runs until stopped with Ctrl + C
Handles multiple clients concurrently (thread-per-client model)
💻 3. Run the Client

In a new terminal:

python3 Client.py
Connects to localhost:5000 by default
Supports multiple simultaneous clients
Interactive CLI-based requests
🧪 4. Run Automated Tests

With server running:

python3 Tests.py
Executes 21 predefined test cases
Covers valid inputs + error handling
🔄 Supported Command Format
CONVERT <CATEGORY> <FROM_UNIT> <TO_UNIT> <VALUE>
Category	Units	Example
TEMP	C, F	CONVERT TEMP C F 25
LENGTH	KM, MI	CONVERT LENGTH KM MI 10
WEIGHT	KG, LB	CONVERT WEIGHT KG LB 5
CURRENCY	USD, CAD, EUR, GBP	CONVERT CURRENCY USD CAD 100
Commands are case-insensitive
Type EXIT or QUIT to disconnect client
💬 Example Session
Enter request: CONVERT TEMP C F 25
Server response: RESULT 77.00 F

Enter request: CONVERT CURRENCY USD CAD 100
Server response: RESULT 137.00 CAD

Enter request: CONVERT FOO C F 25
Server response: ERROR Invalid category

Enter request: EXIT
Connection closed.
❌ Error Handling
Condition	Response
Unknown category	ERROR Invalid category
Invalid unit for category	ERROR Invalid unit
Non-numeric value	ERROR Invalid numeric value
Malformed request	ERROR Malformed request
📊 Server Logging

Every connection and request is logged:

Client connected: ('127.0.0.1', 55842)
Request: CONVERT TEMP C F 25 → RESULT 77.00 F
Client disconnected: ('127.0.0.1', 55842)
⚠️ Known Limitations
Host/port are hardcoded constants
Currency rates are static (no live API)
Assumes one request per TCP packet (recv-safe design)
No graceful shutdown messaging to clients
No authentication or encryption (educational use only)
🚀 Summary

A simple but powerful networked conversion engine demonstrating:

TCP socket programming
Multithreading
Custom protocol design
Client-server architecture
Automated testing
